## Real Estate Manager

Industrial holdings of Lugano (AIL) SA — open position in Lugano/Muzzano (TI).

AIL SA Casella postale 6901 Lugano Centre Via Industria 2 6933 Muzzano Tel. 058 470 70 www.ail.ch
• info@ail.ch Who we are: We are a dynamic company in the energy sector and in the supply of drinking water, evolving and with a strong focus on innovation and development of people. We are looking for a person with a transversal vision, entrepreneurial approach and strong coordination ability, as Real Estate Manager 80%-100% for support for projects, in the civil building sector, at a time determined until the end of the projects. Your impact: Referring directly to the President of the Management you will be the reference figure to analyze, define and accompany strategic choices on our real estate assets (sales, development, requalification, maintenance to income), ensuring economic and financial sustainability, correct governance of the projects and an effective dialogue with the main stakeholders. You will work as a representative of the client in the design groups and ensure the implementation of the projects along the entire life cycle, from the initial idea to realization. What you will do concretely:
• evaluate the strategic options for each property/asset: disposal, valorization, development, requalification, income maintenance, with comparative analysis of scenarios;
• you will establish and validate the economic and financial sustainability of operations: business plan, expected returns, sensitivities, cost structure, embroidery/location hypothesis, financing methods;
• you will coordinate the project ecosystem: designers, consultants, enterprises, experts, authorities and institutions, ensuring timeliness, quality and decision-making consistency;
• you will represent AIL as a contractor in design groups (civil, thermo-sanitary, electrical, fire specialist and other skills), ensuring clarity on requirements, priorities and constraints;
• you will ensure the correct implementation of the projects: progress, milestone, risk management, variants, quality, compliance with technical and regulatory requirements, cost/time control;
• you will manage complex projects from the stage of idea and feasibility to design, permits, race/assegnations, execution, testing and commissioning;
• you will preside over the local context (Ticinese market): dynamic demand / supply, urban addresses, relationship with operators and institutions, with ability to read opportunities and constraints to increase the probability of success. Who are you?
• you have a training as civil architect/engineer (or similar), or continuous specialization in Real Estate (preferential title);
• you have a solid foundation in real estate and demonstrate the ability to integrate economic, financial and technical aspects;
• you have an entrepreneurial approach and solutions-oriented: analyze each asset as a specific opportunity and choose the most efficient option without predefined schemes;
• you are a structured, autonomous and reliable person;
• brings an important experience in managing real estate operations and/or development/requalification projects, with responsibility for coordination and relationship with external stakeholders;
• know the local context and you are familiar with market dynamics, operators and local institutions;
• you have excellent communication, negotiation and synthesis skills;
• you have excellent knowledge of the Italian language; knowledge of a second national language and/or English is a preferential title;
• you have Swiss citizenship or a residence permit. What we offer:
• an important role in a consolidated and evolving society;
• a collaborative working environment, with ample space to bring ideas and innovation;
• possibility to grow professionally, acquiring new skills and responsibilities;
• flexibility and support to reconcile professional and personal life;
• possibility of further training and continuing training;
• Contractual conditions, insurance and social security. AIL SA Casella postale 6901 Lugano Centre Via Industria 2 6933 Muzzano Tel. 058 470 70 www.ail.ch
• info@ail.ch Attachment documents:
• motivational letter;
• complete dossier of curriculum vitae, diplomas and work certificates;
• copy of the identity document. At a later date, an excerpt from the execution and bankruptcy office will be required and an updated judicial checkout with a maximum validity of 3 months. End of the competition: Friday 31 July 2026. Please fill in the online application attached to the competition. We will carefully evaluate each dossier.

** Application deadline:** 2026-08-01

**Sector:** Energy / Public Services

**Sede:** Via Industria 2, 6933 Muzzano (Lugano), TI, Switzerland

[Official note (PDF)](https://www.ail.ch/downloadJobPosition?uuid=8e7b657d-9952-4d94-bca4-a284b97f30e3)

